From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 19:31:13 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] zink: support Venus implicit native dma-bufs

DRM format modifiers are offered to common WSI only where the renderer has no
native heap to share. A surface that offers modifiers takes common WSI's
explicit-modifier path, which filters the modifiers through a colour
attachment format query and presents whichever linear layout survives. On a
paired Metal renderer that replaces the zero-copy native scanout this topic
exists to provide with a linear presented image the compositor has to
reinterpret. The policy sits beside the native envelope it belongs with, as a
header-only predicate the native test covers.
